      "abstained": false,
      "answer": "**The passages don't give a general rule for respiratory protection in an airborne infection isolation room, but they do cover some specific diseases.**\n\n- **Measles:** Staff should use respiratory protection at least as protective as a fit-tested, NIOSH-certified N95 respirator when entering the patient's room, whatever their immunity. Another passage disagrees, stating there are no data on which to base a respiratory protection recommendation for measles or varicella-zoster.\n- **SARS:** Airborne Precautions include fit-tested NIOSH-approved N95 or higher-level respirators.",
